note effects probe for enlarge (check.sh probe parity, probes.txt `enlarge|@probe-enlarge.om`): enlarge is
note only the whole of an assignment to a run-time pool, so it cannot sit in the `r = long EXPR` probe.
note The first growth maps the pool (mmap 222); the omc_enlarge helper also holds the mremap (216).
global P ulong *
fn main to int
r = enlarge P ulong 4
ret 0
end
note gate-pools: uses enlarge on purpose: owner=seed/effects/check.sh effects probe parity
